                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lark",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32202be9-a1d8-3c69-b5b2-cebe028f1cd4",
                                        "entry_id": "c232718e-997e-34e9-bedd-5ab20c5e8bc5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A frolic or romp, some fun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9aa1ee83-6f3f-4fb8-b2f6-0c24a8c8dfa3",
                                                "sense_id": "32202be9-a1d8-3c69-b5b2-cebe028f1cd4",
                                                "text": "‘Ha! ha!’ laughed Master Bates, ‘what a lark that would be, wouldn’t it, Fagin? I say, how the Artful would bother ’em wouldn’t he?’"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "207b9b0f-6134-470a-8cd1-09a9c11f4f81",
                                                "sense_id": "32202be9-a1d8-3c69-b5b2-cebe028f1cd4",
                                                "text": "“Oh, dear, no,” said the young Englishman; “my cousin was coming over on some business, so I just came across, at an hour’s notice, for the lark.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23d4bce5-fc46-4986-b1c3-6af0874c197e",
                                                "sense_id": "32202be9-a1d8-3c69-b5b2-cebe028f1cd4",
                                                "text": "Thanks partly to Tom Wolfe’s raised-eyebrow account, “The Electric Kool-Aid Acid Test,” that bohemian lark has been retrospectively hailed as the flash point of the emerging hippie counterculture."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d09a6f9b-3d4d-4379-b13a-fa37b38bb04a",
                                                "sense_id": "32202be9-a1d8-3c69-b5b2-cebe028f1cd4",
                                                "text": "What began as a lark has grown into something very, very big, inflating the company’s ambitions."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6db811dd-c45d-37fb-9255-0bb0d671c2d9",
                                        "entry_id": "c232718e-997e-34e9-bedd-5ab20c5e8bc5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A prank."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31f28ccb-c4ba-46ef-80d7-7165f47e4e4c",
                                                "sense_id": "6db811dd-c45d-37fb-9255-0bb0d671c2d9",
                                                "text": "doolittle. […] [T]hanks to your silly joking, he leaves me a share in his Pre-digested Cheese Trust worth three thousand a year on condition that I lecture for his Wannafeller Moral Reform World League as often as they ask me up to six times a year. / higgins. The devil he does! Whew! [Brightening suddenly] What a lark!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lark",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2d2c88d2-8bff-3517-9427-3f669a70997a",
                                        "entry_id": "43669089-0f56-3d30-9b77-8add57d53824",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To sport, engage in harmless pranking."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84d56c6b-dc8c-4253-97ba-86bb33599c34",
                                                "sense_id": "2d2c88d2-8bff-3517-9427-3f669a70997a",
                                                "text": "[T]hey laugh at us old boys,” thought old Pendennis. And he was not far wrong; the times and manners which he admired were pretty nearly gone—the gay young men “larked” him irreverently […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "643fb3f4-3edb-490e-8345-ae243b122a80",
                                                "sense_id": "2d2c88d2-8bff-3517-9427-3f669a70997a",
                                                "text": "[…] the porter at the rail-road had seen a scuffle; or when he found it was likely to bring him in as a witness, then it might not have been a scuffle, only a little larking […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
